kind: binding
semantic_diff: >-
  Instruments on five existing nodes, declared per node; no node, outcome, edge,
  check, or evidence definition changes and the counts stay 32 / 95 / 15. (0)
  Seat continuity for the stage-6 loop, declared once per node in activities
  (where revision 2 put its instruments): one retained doer thread per campaign
  answers scope_next_increment (when a seat is dispatched), realize_increment,
  and record_changeset for every item, replaced only when its context degrades
  the work; review_increment_batch stays a fresh seat per batch. (1)
  scope_next_increment: every lap the lead settles mechanically from the
  persisted inputs (landed set, gate table and milestone order, ascending id,
  open batch and size call, detector inputs, worktree preconditions) with a lap
  record that carries the commands it derived from; the implementer seat runs
  only for a judgment the rule does not settle - a contradiction candidate no
  realizer record holds, or a findings-history versus lap-record disagreement;
  ambiguity runs the seat. (2) review_campaign_design re-entry: whole read on
  the first review of a design entry and on full-lap re-entries; after a
  block-scoped repair the seat reads the touched blocks, their cascade, and one
  scripted census while the lead byte-checks untouched blocks against the
  must-hold digests; at the bound re-entry (design_loop_within_bound failed) no
  reviewer seat is dispatched - the lead and the user answer it; the challenger
  is retained across the rounds of one design entry (spec 9.4). (3) assemble_design_record: when the only changed input is a
  verified block diff whose touched blocks keep their contracts complete, the
  lead performs the delta and the self-check with no seat; any other changed
  input, a gap, or ambiguity runs the assembler. (4) realize_increment: one
  retained seat realizes a set in order by default; a concurrent-eligible set
  may run one seat per item when each has its own checkout and the lead lands
  them at the join, a join conflict returning the set to serial. Price per run:
  the scoper seat goes from one per lap to one per judgment lap; a bookkeeping
  reviewer round and an assembler seat per block-scoped re-entry go to zero;
  no new seat is priced. Envelope (rule 6) - changed_with_approval: the lap
  record becomes the lead's by default and the lead performs the record delta -
  state-authority moves under rule 6. Same checks, cheaper instruments,
  mechanical evidence still produced in every lap record (rule 9's bound); a
  check the graph forbids the lead to judge keeps its seat. Why it
  holds in general: an outcome any reader re-derives from persisted inputs is
  not a judgment, so a seat that re-derives it buys no evidence, and a fresh
  challenger each round forces a living document to carry its whole argument
  history in self-defense.
envelope_check: changed_with_approval
plan_evidence: verified
usage_evidence: field
changelog_entry: >-
  Revision 4 (binding): one retained doer thread per campaign across the
  stage-6 loop nodes, lead-mechanical scoping with a conditional implementer
  seat, delta-scoped gate-2 re-review with a retained challenger, a
  lead-performed record delta on a verified block diff, and the hands-per-set
  rule for realization. Field evidence from the first run: across 51 scoping
  laps the priced no_new_route outcome never fired and 49 laps were a
  re-derivable selection; the scoper seat was cut to lead-mechanical from lap 52
  and the lap record shrank to about fifteen lines; the record assembler re-ran
  as a seat on every narrow re-entry; a fresh implementer seat was opened per
  increment, so each re-read the design record from zero.
